# All-sky plate carree, CRVAL2 = 0, no LONPOLE card: wcslib's default
# LONPOLE for a cylindrical projection with delta0 >= theta0 (= 0) is
# phi0 = 0. Pixel grid runs 20 px past every edge of the 720x360 map, so
# |x| > 180 deg and |y| > 90 deg intermediate coordinates are exercised
# and the rejection status must agree with wcslib.
#
# Sky points avoid the two places where the sky->pixel answer is
# multi-valued, so a pixel difference there would not be a bug: the poles
# (every pixel along y = 0.5 / 360.5 is the pole) and the seam at
# lng = CRVAL1 +- 180 = 0/360 (x = 0.5 and x = 720.5 are the same sky).
# Explicit pixels likewise stay off the map border.
NOTE smoke: CAR all-sky, default LONPOLE, grid past the map edges
GRID -19.5 740.5 20 -19.5 380.5 17
PIX 1 1
PIX 720 360
PIX 360.5 180.5
SKYGRID 1 359 13 -89 89 13
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 720
NAXIS2  = 360
CTYPE1  = 'RA---CAR'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--CAR'
CRVAL1  = 180.0
CRVAL2  = 0.0
CRPIX1  = 360.5
CRPIX2  = 180.5
CDELT1  = -0.5
CDELT2  = 0.5
